==================================================================================
simulate_herschel.py — SPIRE 350 um, GPD tail statistics of the CIB
==================================================================================
simulate_herschel.py — Herschel/SPIRE 350 um arm of the GPD/CIB-lensing suite
==============================================================================

Unlensed xi(u) and cluster-lensed Delta_xi(u) for Herschel-SPIRE at 350 um,
with every instrument parameter taken from the measured GAMA-09 analysis rather
than from a scaling of the count model.

Supersedes the Herschel panels of `main_sims_unlensed.py` and
`main_sims_lensed.py`.  All changes implement recommendations of
`instrument_consistency_audit.md` (2026-08-15); the audit tag is given for each.
==================================================================================
Herschel — noise budget at S_min = 1.0 mJy (audit R1), S_cut = 100 mJy
==================================================================================
  <Herschel: 25.15" beam, 8.0" pix, sigma_N=5.402, S_cut=100 mJy>
  provenance: Full_Analysis_Summary_Herschel.md: beam 25.15" (Matchedfilter header, Condon-equivalent); pixel 8.0" (HELP map); sigma_N 5.402 mJy/beam (matched filter, 11.3% cutout scatter); no non-Poisson term needed (model+noise matches SF_IMAGE rms to 7%)

     model   sigma_c   sigma_N  sigma_nonP  Sigma_tot    N_beam    skew  s_split  f_N impl
 Schechter      7.98      5.40         0.0       9.63       4.8    1.77     1.00     0.677
       SPL     10.01      5.40         0.0      11.37      33.9    0.95     1.00     0.540
       DPL      7.58      5.40         0.0       9.31       2.0    2.08     1.00     0.712

  measured core width = 9.00 mJy/beam;  simulated (Schechter) = 9.63  -> ratio 1.070
  counts fitted over S = 6.0-94.6 mJy; NO renormalisation applied anywhere (audit R4).

  Cross-checks against the measured GAMA-09 decomposition (H3 Sec. 5.5):
    measured total rms 9.003, minus sigma_N 5.402 -> sky rms 7.202 mJy/beam
    model sigma_c (Schechter)          7.976  -> model/measured 1.107
    Nguyen et al. (2010) 350 um: sigma_conf = 6.3 +- 0.4 mJy/beam (plain pixel variance,
      24.9" beam, effective cut ~80 mJy).  Our model is 25% high there; the CUT DEPENDENCE
      is reproduced to 4% (audit Sec. 5.2), so the offset is an amplitude and is 1.1 sigma
      of the joint counts-normalisation ⊕ SPIRE-calibration uncertainty.  NOT corrected.
