Herschel — pixel-scale diagnostic (audit R5)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The data run at FWHM/pix = 25.15/8.0 = 3.14, outside the 4-10 range over which
  the declustering peak-density calibration was established, and the measured peak
  density (0.374/beam) exceeds the old 5" simulation's (0.252/beam) by 48%.  Here the
  same unlensed run is repeated at 5" to isolate the pixelisation effect from the
  physical one (source clustering, which raises the real density above Poisson).
